+## Current source and uncertainty
+
+A shared lookup retains the actual source, complete profile/configuration,
+registry selection and document revision. Provider publication and edit
+application must rejoin that current owner; a name, range or display label
+cannot reconstruct it. Navigation and edits may have different proof purposes:
+a source-only relationship does not grant runtime binding or rewrite authority.
+
+Unproven cross-document execution order, replaced bindings, stale analysis and
+opaque effects remain unavailable. Providers preserve that uncertainty rather
+than choosing a convenient candidate. ILX source tracking ends at an opaque
+remote operation; later notifications do not restore the earlier handle binding.
+The [capabilities page](../../capabilities.md#source-aware-editor-behaviour-and-execution-limits)
+states these limits for users, including profile-specific execution support and
+the deferred general VM/backend parity boundary.
 
